{"name":"Walleye","hex":"#9b5953","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"walleye","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One or a pair of sideways-looking misaligned eyes.","An unusually pale eye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walleye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Walleye","blocks":[{"text":"The walleye, also called the walleyed pike, yellow pike, yellow pikeperch or yellow pickerel, is a freshwater perciform fish native to most of Canada and to the Northern United States. It is a North American close relative of the European zander, also known as the pikeperch. The walleye is sometimes called the yellow walleye to distinguish it from the blue walleye, which is a color morph that was once found in the southern Ontario and Quebec regions, but is now presumed extinct. However, recent genetic analysis of a preserved (frozen) 'blue walleye' sample suggests that the blue and yellow walleye were simply phenotypes within the same species and do not merit separate taxonomic classification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Walleye_%28Sander_vitreus%29_%281%29.jpg/330px-Walleye_%28Sander_vitreus%29_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walleye"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sander_vitreus.jpg/500px-Sander_vitreus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sander_vitreus.jpg/1280px-Sander_vitreus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sander_vitreus.jpg/500px-Sander_vitreus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Walleye (Sander vitreus)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASander_vitreus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w